<!-- About -->
<section id="about" class="section">

    <div class="section-title">
        <p>ABOUT ME</p>
        <h2>Researching economics<br>for a changing world.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="about-content">

        <div>
            <p>
                I am an economist and researcher from Bangladesh with an
                academic background in Economics from Khulna University.
            </p>

            <p>
                My research interests lie at the intersection of
                environmental economics, development economics and public
                policy, particularly issues related to climate change,
                environmental vulnerability and rural livelihoods.
            </p>

            <p>
                I am particularly interested in understanding how
                environmental and economic changes affect vulnerable
                communities and how better policies can support sustainable
                development.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="quick-info">

            <div>
                <span>Education</span>
                <strong>Khulna University</strong>
            </div>

            <div>
                <span>Field</span>
                <strong>Economics</strong>
            </div>

            <div>
                <span>Location</span>
                <strong>Khulna, Bangladesh</strong>
            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</section>


<!-- Research -->
<section id="research" class="section dark-section">

    <div class="section-title">
        <p>RESEARCH</p>
        <h2>Research & Projects</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="research-grid">

        <article class="research-card">

            <span class="number">01</span>

            <h3>Impact of River Degradation on Rural Livelihoods in Khulna</h3>

            <p>
                Master's thesis examining the effects of river degradation
                on rural livelihoods, occupational change and household
                income.
            </p>

            <span class="tag">Master's Thesis</span>

        </article>


        <article class="research-card">

            <span class="number">02</span>

            <h3>Managing Saline-Free Drinking Water and Multidimensional Poverty</h3>

            <p>
                Research project investigating the relationship between
                safe drinking water scarcity and multidimensional poverty
                in coastal Bangladesh.
            </p>

            <span class="tag">Data Analysis</span>

        </article>


        <article class="research-card">

            <span class="number">03</span>

            <h3>Farmers' Behavioral Drivers to Adopt Floating Farming</h3>

            <p>
                Field research examining farmers' behavioral drivers and
                adoption of floating farming in wetlands of southwestern
                coastal Bangladesh.
            </p>

            <span class="tag">Field Research</span>

        </article>


        <article class="research-card">

            <span class="number">04</span>

            <h3>Climate Finance and Local-Level Adaptation</h3>

            <p>
                Research examining the climate finance gap in Bangladesh
                and the importance of transparency, decentralization and
                accountability.
            </p>

            <span class="tag">Climate Policy</span>

        </article>

    </div>

</section>


<!-- Publications -->
<section id="publications" class="section">

    <div class="section-title">
        <p>PUBLICATIONS</p>
        <h2>Selected Research</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="publication">

        <div class="publication-year">
            2026
        </div>

        <div>
            <h3>
                The climate finance gap in Bangladesh: Are we spending
                enough on local-level adaptation?
            </h3>

            <p>
                Nishe, S. N., Chowdhury, N. A., & Mohanta, A. K.
            </p>

            <p class="journal">
                Development Letters, 7(1), Research and Policy Integration
                for Development (RAPID).
            </p>

            <p>
                Investigates local-level climate finance gaps and discusses
                the need for greater transparency, fiscal decentralization
                and accountability.
            </p>
        </div>

    </div>


    <div class="publication">

        <div class="publication-year">
            2026
        </div>

        <div>

